| Script | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| `npm run dev` | Start development server |
| `npm run build` | Build for production |
| `npm run preview` | Preview production build |
| `npm run typecheck` | Run TypeScript compiler check |
| `npm run lint` | Lint and auto-fix with ESLint |
| `npm run format` | Format code with Prettier |
| `npm run storybook` | Start Storybook dev server |
| `npm run storybook:build` | Build Storybook for deployment |

## Project Structure

```
src/
├── theme/           # Design tokens and theme configuration
├── shared/
│   ├── ui/          # Reusable UI components
│   └── lib/         # Utility functions
├── features/        # Feature modules
├── hooks/           # Shared React hooks
├── routes/          # File-based routes (TanStack Router)
└── main.tsx         # Application entry point
```

## Architecture

This project follows a layered architecture with enforced import boundaries:

- **theme/** - Design tokens (colors, typography, spacing). Leaf layer with no imports.
- **shared/lib/** - Pure utility functions with no dependencies.
- **shared/ui/** - Reusable UI components. Can import from theme and shared/lib.
- **features/** - Feature-specific modules. Can import from theme and shared, but not other features.
- **hooks/** - Shared React hooks. Can import from theme and shared/lib.
- **routes/** - Page components. Can import from all layers.

ESLint enforces these boundaries automatically.

## Design System

This project uses a token-based design system built on Ant Design. Never hardcode colors, fonts, or spacing values.

```tsx
import { useDesignTokens } from '@/theme'

function MyComponent() {
  const { token } = useDesignTokens()

  return (
    <div style={{
      color: token.colorPrimary,
      padding: token.padding
    }}>
      Hello
    </div>
  )
}
```

See `src/theme/tokens/` for available tokens.

## Storybook

Develop and document UI components in isolation:

```bash
npm run storybook
```

Opens at [http://localhost:6006](http://localhost:6006).

Components in `src/shared/ui/` include stories for interactive documentation and visual testing.

## Adding Routes

Create a new file in `src/routes/`:

```tsx
// src/routes/about.tsx
import { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'

export const Route = createFileRoute('/about')({
  component: AboutPage,
})

function AboutPage() {
  return <div>About</div>
}
```

Routes are automatically registered when the dev server is running.

